WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:04.840
- You may have been
rejected by your family

00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:06.500
because you're LGBT,

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:10.139
so our Thanksgiving celebration
is a way to celebrate

00:00:10.139 --> 00:00:12.930
our family that we've
built here at the center

00:00:12.930 --> 00:00:15.530
and for everyone to have the opportunity

00:00:15.530 --> 00:00:17.703
to be supported during the holidays.

00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:20.690
- I'm Nico Tortorella.

00:00:20.690 --> 00:00:22.270
I'm an actor, an activist,

00:00:22.270 --> 00:00:23.440
and a firm believer

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:26.320
that our differences
actually make us stronger.

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:28.930
I'm on a journey with
IKEA to meet real people

00:00:28.930 --> 00:00:31.549
and discover the diverse
and spectacular ways

00:00:31.549 --> 00:00:33.573
they celebrate the holidays.

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:40.330
Maybe you celebrate Thanksgiving
with your extended family

00:00:40.330 --> 00:00:41.920
and maybe you celebrate Thanksgiving

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:45.299
with your chosen family, like
the people at our first stop.

00:00:45.299 --> 00:00:47.780
- I'm David Mariner, and
I'm the Executive Director

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:50.890
of The DC Center for the LGBT Community.

00:00:50.890 --> 00:00:54.050
Welcome to our Fifth Annual
Thanksgiving Celebration.

00:00:54.050 --> 00:00:57.260
Everyone comes with their own experiences

00:00:57.260 --> 00:00:59.453
and traditions and customs.

00:01:00.940 --> 00:01:04.940
We need to acknowledge not
just their LGBT identities,

00:01:04.940 --> 00:01:07.150
but their whole self.

00:01:07.150 --> 00:01:08.800
- My name is Nikilas Mawanda.

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:09.910
I'm originally from Uganda

00:01:09.910 --> 00:01:11.940
but right now living in Washington, D.C.

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:15.890
- [Nico] The DC Center
helps LGBTQ+ asylum seekers

00:01:15.890 --> 00:01:19.770
and refugees who are no longer
safe in their own countries.

00:01:19.770 --> 00:01:22.280
- It's commonplace for
someone to be kicked

00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:26.330
out of their home in Uganda for LGBT.

00:01:26.330 --> 00:01:28.610
It's commonplace for someone

00:01:28.610 --> 00:01:31.660
to be disowned by their family.

00:01:31.660 --> 00:01:33.530
- [Nico] This year the
asylum seekers and refugees

00:01:33.530 --> 00:01:36.640
are bringing a traditional
dish from their home country

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:38.770
to share with the entire center.

00:01:38.770 --> 00:01:40.893
Nik is preparing rolexes.

00:01:41.870 --> 00:01:44.090
It's called rolex in Uganda, too?

00:01:44.090 --> 00:01:47.297
- Yes, and it's just the way we roll it.

00:01:47.297 --> 00:01:48.130
- Ahh.

00:01:49.070 --> 00:01:51.200
- It is really important
for me that I share

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:53.380
the beautiful thing about my culture.

00:01:53.380 --> 00:01:56.993
We celebrate brotherhood,
sisterhood, in forms of sharing.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:02.130
- Knife is on the inside or the outside?

00:02:02.130 --> 00:02:03.689
- Knife is on the inside.

00:02:03.689 --> 00:02:04.522
- OK.

00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:08.040
- Hi everyone, I'm Tamara.

00:02:08.040 --> 00:02:11.460
My pronouns are she, her, and hers.

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:15.570
My tradition actually has
been coming to the DC Center

00:02:15.570 --> 00:02:18.060
to volunteer and give back.

00:02:18.060 --> 00:02:20.800
- [Nico] I think when we go
around the table and we share

00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:23.260
the traditions that we
have around the holidays,

00:02:23.260 --> 00:02:25.700
we all are a little bit more connected

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:29.550
and we understand how similar we all are.

00:02:29.550 --> 00:02:32.910
- My favorite holiday tradition is eating.

00:02:32.910 --> 00:02:34.210
(group laughing)

00:02:34.210 --> 00:02:39.210
And second only by being
around my friends and family.

00:02:39.570 --> 00:02:41.980
- I grew up in Nebraska, and we always had

00:02:41.980 --> 00:02:45.133
a Thanksgiving dinner like,
not too different than this.

00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:48.720
- [Nik] I would love to share

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:50.620
the good things about my tradition.

00:02:50.620 --> 00:02:53.410
People won't learn unless you share,

00:02:53.410 --> 00:02:55.744
it's part of bringing cross-cultures.

00:02:56.353 --> 00:02:58.310
It's part of learning about each other,

00:02:58.310 --> 00:02:59.563
appreciating each other.

00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:02.620
- [Nico] We celebrate differently,

00:03:02.620 --> 00:03:05.063
but maybe that's what
makes us all so beautiful.

00:03:06.710 --> 00:03:10.560
It's more important today
than ever to show up

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:13.260
for the holidays as yourself.

00:03:13.260 --> 00:03:15.750
Share your tradition, 'cause
the more that we see,

00:03:15.750 --> 00:03:18.180
the more we believe, the more we respect,

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:19.930
and the more we love.

